`src/usage.js` adapts the per-day, per-model token-usage fold from
`dsh-usage-stats/lib/usage.js`, retaining its dual-source sampling
(`assistant/chunk` + `assistant/message`), its same-(turn, step) replacement
semantics, and its `message.source` → `request/header` route attribution.
TokenLedger extends that fold with a relay-site dimension, reasoning-token and
request counting, disjoint-bucket billed totals, and range/site queries.

This product's understanding of the DSH event contract is derived from the
published type declarations of the following MIT-licensed packages, which are
not redistributed here:

